{"nodes": [{"id": "packages_db_readme_arcula_db", "label": "@arcula/db Schema Package", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_schema_single_source_of_truth", "label": "Schema as Single Source of Truth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "src/index.ts is imported by the API over a live driver, read by drizzle-kit to generate migrations, and asserted by tests. A table added by hand outside the schema is still open because RLS defaults to off \u2014 one reason the schema stays the single source of truth."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_better_auth_core_tables", "label": "Better Auth Core Tables", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "user, session, account and verification, with user extended by the four typed custom columns firstName, lastName, tier and settings that the API declares to the adapter."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_domain_tables", "label": "Nine Domain Tables", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_forward_only_migrations", "label": "Forward-Only Migrations", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gerated SQL is committed and applied, never reversed; hand edits are limited to three documented cases (a data backfill appended after generation, because drizzle-kit renders schema and never data; the add-nullable \u2192 backfill \u2192 set-not-null sequence; and a grant revoke drizzle-kit cannot model). Nothing else is edited by hand."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_data_backfill_hand_edit", "label": "Data Backfill Hand Edit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_add_nullable_backfill_not_null", "label": "Add-Nullable \u2192 Backfill \u2192 Set-Not-Null", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A column that cannot be added NOT NULL on an existing table is added nullable, backfilled, and tightened afterwards, split across releases so old code stays valid in between."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_0003_shared_collections", "label": "0003_shared_collections Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Creates the two sharing tables, replaces the owner-list index and adds mediaNamespaceId nullable backfilled from userId; it shipped alone, the feature code followed, and 0004 tightened the column afterwards."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_0004_media_namespace_not_null", "label": "0004_media_namespace_not_null Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backfills only the rows the old code wrote in between (WHERE mediaNamespaceId IS NULL, so a namespace the new code minted survives) and then sets the column NOT NULL."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_0005_collection_passwords", "label": "0005_collection_passwords Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adds collections.passwordHash nullable and creates the two password tables; it needs no tightening step because a collection without a password is the normal state rather than a gap to backfill."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_0006_enable_rls", "label": "0006_enable_rls Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "enableRLS() makes drizzle-kit generate the thirteen ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY statements, but a grant lives in Postgres's ACL and not in the schema declaration, so the guarded DO block revoking anon and authenticated is appended by hand. The guard is deliberate: Supabase creates those roles while the local stack and CI have neither, so an unguarded REVOKE FROM anon would fail every db:migrate with role \"anon\" does not exist."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_rls_lockdown", "label": "RLS Lock-down with Zero Policies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every table enables RLS with zero policies so the PostgREST roles see nothing; the API connects as the table owner, which bypasses RLS, so the lock-down is invisible to the product. FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY must never be added, because it would subject the owner to the empty policy set and blank every read."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_supabase_admin_default_acl", "label": "Accepted supabase_admin Default-ACL Residue (#181)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES is per-grantor: 0006 runs as postgres, which is not a member of supabase_admin, so the platform's second book of defaults survives and supabase_admin keeps full grants for both client roles on tables and sequences it creates. The residue is accepted because every table in the schema is created by drizzle-kit migrate as postgres, so the product's own path starts closed, and the surviving grants become reachable only with the Data API enabled and a table created in public by supabase_admin outside the schema. Closing it would be dashboard state, not repository state."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_timestamptz_decision", "label": "timestamptz Everywhere", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_money_as_text", "label": "Money Stored as text", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Money is the string that was typed, so there is no float drift."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_deleted_at_soft_delete", "label": "deletedAt NULL Means Live", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_photo_variant_upsert", "label": "artwork_photo_variants (parentId, key) Upsert", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keying on (parentId, key) is what makes a re-save an idempotent upsert."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_owner_fact", "label": "collections.userId as the One Owner Fact", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A collaborator is a row in collection_collaborators and the owner is not duplicated there; artworks.userId is a mirror of the collection owner, not an authorization fact."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_media_namespace_id", "label": "collections.mediaNamespaceId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed at creation, so an ownership transfer moves no object and existing URLs keep working."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_pending_invitation_partial_index", "label": "Partial Unique Pending-Invitation Index", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "collection_invitations stores the token's hash, never the token, with one pending offer per collection and address enforced as a partial unique index."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_password_hash_column", "label": "collections.passwordHash", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nullable, holding a one-way hash with its salt and parameters in the string \u2014 no read-back and no default."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_access_grants_table", "label": "collection_access_grants Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeps a grant's hash, never its token, with the collection indexed so a password change revokes in one statement."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_unlock_attempts_table", "label": "collection_unlock_attempts Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written and read by the unlock route alone, which is the throttle's whole surface."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_structural_contract_tests", "label": "Structural Contract Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assert the in-memory schema and the committed migration against each other's ground truth \u2014 table shapes, CHECKs, the artwork-list indexes, the collaborator userId index, the partial unique pending-invitation index, the nullable \u2192 backfill \u2192 NOT NULL order, timestamptz, defaults, and the lock-down (RLS on all thirteen tables plus the guarded revoke and the absence of FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY)."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_runtime_free_schema", "label": "Runtime-Free Schema", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No driver, no driver-specific types, no DOM: the package's tests read the migration off disk so Node types are available, and the DOM-free guarantee is the tsconfig lib array. @arcula/shared is the client-contract side of the same wall."}], "edges": [{"source": "packages_db_readme_arcula_db", "target": "packages_db_readme_schema_single_source_of_truth", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_arcula_db", "target": "docs_adr_0004_collections_are_shared_by_membership_membership_sharing", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_arcula_db", "target": "docs_adr_0005_a_password_is_a_second_condition_on_a_public_collection_access_grant", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_better_auth_core_tables", "target": "packages_db_readme_domain_tables", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_arcula_db", "target": "packages_db_readme_better_auth_core_tables", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_arcula_db", "target": "packages_db_readme_domain_tables", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_domain_tables", "target": "packages_db_readme_owner_fact", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_domain_tables", "target": "packages_db_readme_pending_invitation_partial_index", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_forward_only_migrations", "target": "packages_db_readme_data_backfill_hand_edit", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_forward_only_migrations", "target": "packages_db_readme_add_nullable_backfill_not_null", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_forward_only_migrations", "target": "packages_db_readme_0006_enable_rls", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_add_nullable_backfill_not_null", "target": "packages_db_readme_0003_shared_collections", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_add_nullable_backfill_not_null", "target": "packages_db_readme_0004_media_namespace_not_null", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_0003_shared_collections", "target": "packages_db_readme_0004_media_namespace_not_null", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_0003_shared_collections", "target": "packages_db_readme_media_namespace_id", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_0003_shared_collections", "target": "docs_adr_0004_collections_are_shared_by_membership_membership_sharing", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_db_readme_0005_collection_passwords", "target": "docs_adr_0005_a_password_is_a_second_condition_on_a_public_collection_access_grant", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "